---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Brand from '../components/Brand';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Field Relay — reconciliation case study</title>
    <link rel="icon" href={base + 'favicon.svg'} type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="case-study">
      <header class="masthead">
        <Brand href={base} /><nav aria-label="Case study navigation">
          <a href={base + 'walkthrough/'}>Interview walkthrough</a><a href={base}>Compare files</a>
        </nav>
      </header>
      <p class="eyebrow">FIELD RELAY / CASE STUDY</p>
      <h1>Spot the differences between two order sheets.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A supplier sends a new spreadsheet. Before you use it, you need to know what changed. Field
        Relay compares it with your existing file and shows the rows that need a closer look.
      </p>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Load two CSV files, choose the ID column in each, and pick the columns you want to compare.
        The app finds changed values, missing orders and repeated or blank IDs. It keeps IDs exactly
        as written, so 0007 and 7 are treated as different IDs.
      </p>
      <h2>Check the original rows</h2>
      <p>
        Open a result to see both source rows. You can hold it for follow-up, mark a difference as
        expected, or suggest using the second file’s value when there is one clear match. Add a
        reason and save the review. The app does not choose for you when an ID is missing or
        repeated.
      </p>
      <h2>Keep a copy of your review</h2>
      <p>
        Download a CSV list of the findings or a JSON review pack with the source files, comparison
        settings and your decisions. Changing either file or the comparison settings clears your
        reviews, because they may no longer apply.
      </p>
      <h2>Try a failed delivery</h2>
      <p>
        The delivery simulator is a separate demo with made-up orders. You can cause an outage, try
        again and check that repeating a delivered order does not create another one. It does not
        use your comparison results or send anything to a real supplier.
      </p>
      <h2>Your files stay in the tab</h2>
      <p>
        Files you select or paste are processed in your browser. They are not uploaded. The sample
        data is made up, but you can compare your own CSV files. Download your work before closing
        the tab; it is not saved automatically.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={base}>Compare two files</a> · <a href={base.replace(/\/?$/, '/') + 'walkthrough/'}
          >Interview walkthrough</a
        > · <a href="https://github.com/mastodonsharkgirl/field-relay">View the code</a>
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
